{"chunk_id": "be38b11f336a", "text": "While Rama attends the great sacrifice, the young ascetic singers Kusha and Lava recite a magnificent epic recounting Rama\u2019s own life. When offered gold, they refuse it, explaining that ascetics who live on fruits and roots have no need for wealth. Intrigued, Rama asks about the poem and learns that the sage Valmiki composed it\u2014twenty\u2011four thousand verses narrating his entire life. As the chanting continues over several days, Rama gradually realizes that the boys are Sita\u2019s sons. Reflecting deeply, he sends messengers to Valmiki requesting that Sita appear and publicly attest to her purity before the assembled sages and kings. Valmiki agrees. Rama announces that on the following day Sita will swear her oath before the great assembly, setting the stage for a decisive and emotionally charged moment in the epic.\nRama, realizing the singers are Sita\u2019s sons, orders that Sita appear before the assembly to publicly swear and prove her purity.\nThemes: public honor, purity and reputation, recognition of sons, royal duty vs personal emotion, trial by oath", "vector": [0.01940884068608284, -0.02384590543806553, -0.007220194675028324, 0.004530057776719332, -0.010455001145601273, 0.021667227149009705, -0.031803399324417114, -0.012142148800194263, -0.021959489211440086, -0.019581539556384087, 0.018452346324920654, 0.008116907440125942, -0.005523083731532097, -0.0036167397629469633, -0.010056463070213795, 0.00040269026067107916, 0.04001329839229584, -0.01013617031276226, 0.020484894514083862, -0.004121555481106043, -0.00222351448610425, -0.022344743832945824, -0.013098642230033875, 0.01938227191567421, -0.020936572924256325, -0.0055928281508386135, 0.019847232848405838, -0.028296256437897682, 0.022530727088451385, -0.012879446148872375, -0.010049820877611637, -0.02481568418443203, -0.012713388539850712, -0.002585520502179861, -0.028482241556048393, 0.008980408310890198, -0.003835936076939106, -0.022291604429483414, 0